    "player_hint_1_en": "(E) in the Panic Room, (F) beside a TV and (C) in the Guest Bedroom must occupy C8, C9 and C10 in some order. No one else can fit in C8, C9 or C10.",
    "player_hint_2_en": "(D), beside a shelf, must then be in the Kitchen. (H) is with a woman in the Dining Room. (E), (D), (H) and the woman with (H) all occupy R1, R2, R3 and R4 in some order. In order to fit all four people in these four rows, either (H) or the woman must be in R4 C1. Block the rest of R4 and C1.",
    "player_hint_3_en": "This isolates (B) in the last possible chair for him, R6 C7. This isolates (D) in R2 C6, as (D) can't occupy C8, C9 or C10.",
    "player_hint_4_en": "(A), beside a statue, can only be in R7 C2 or R5 C4. Block the intersecting square R7 C4.",
    "player_hint_5_en": "All the remaining carpet squares are in the Guest Bedroom. (G), one row south of someone on a carpet, must then be in R10. This isolates (C), the only person who can fit on the carpet in the Guest Bedroom, in R9 C8.",
    "player_hint_6_en": "(F) can't fit in the Panic Room between R1 and R3 (see step 2). This isolates (F) in R5 C10 and (E) in the last square in the Panic Room in R3 C9. This isolates (A) in the last square beside a statue in R7 C2.",
    "player_hint_7_en": "This isolates (G) in the last R10 square, R10 C5. (I) must be two columns east of a woman, and the only possibility is if she's two columns east of (V). This sets (V) as the person in R4 C1, (I) in R8 C3, and (H) in R1 C4. (V) was alone with (H), Harold is the murderer!"
  },
